    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1305">

                <pb facs="1131" n="817" xml:id="pg817"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.6741/3</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-14">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 14, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</p>
                <p>540. . . . The President does not think it wise to appoint a committee.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d1305-f1"/> He believes it is better to have the Belgian
                    relief managed by those not officially connected with the Government here. . . .
                    The relief fund is likely to reach some magnitude and we take it for granted
                    that you have examined into the record and standing of Hoover. . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1305-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1305-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph of the Ambassador’s No. 978, November 3, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg814">p. 814</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
